{
  "title": "iOS shopping list / meal plan sync: triggers during a sync can be dropped",
  "description": "ShoppingListStore.triggerSync (281-284) calls syncWithServer, which returns at its !isSyncing guard (302) without setting retryAfterSync (only syncIfNeeded sets it, 288-290). \
Edits made during a sync are picked up only by the post-sync pending check (370), which is skipped when that sync failed or was itself a follow-up, so they wait for the next trigger. \
MealPlanStore has the same shape (triggerSync 188, check at 241). .refreshable { await store.syncWithServer() } returns immediately when a sync is running, so pull-to-refresh can do nothing. \
The two stores have drifted: meal plan has no isOnline guard or published flag, no refreshAfterSync, and syncIfPending vs syncIfNeeded staleness rules differ. \
Want: one sync coordinator (idle / syncing / syncing-with-rerun-queued) shared by both stores, where any trigger during a sync queues a rerun, and pull-to-refresh awaits the in-flight sync. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
